SPECIFICATION:

I would like you to implement a module named TopModule with the following
interface. All input and output ports are one bit unless otherwise
specified.

 - input  clk
 - input  areset
 - input  x
 - output z

The module should implement a one-input one-output serial 2's
complementer Moore state machine. The input (x) is a series of bits (one
per clock cycle) beginning with the least-significant bit of the number,
and the output (Z) is the 2's complement of the input. The machine will
accept input numbers of arbitrary length. The circuit requires a positive
edge triggered asynchronous reset. The conversion begins when Reset is
released and stops when Reset is asserted. Assume all sequential logic is
triggered on the positive edge of the clock.



CANDIDATE RTL TO ATTACK:
```verilog
module TopModule (
    input  wire clk,
    input  wire areset,
    input  wire x,
    output reg  z
);

    // State encoding for the Moore machine:
    // S0: Saw only 0s so far (first '1' hasn't arrived yet)
    // S1: Saw at least one '1' (invert subsequent bits)
    parameter S0 = 1'b0;
    parameter S1 = 1'b1;

    reg state, next_state;

    // Sequential logic: positive edge triggered clock, asynchronous positive-edge reset
    // Wait, the spec says "positive edge triggered asynchronous reset". Standard convention 
    // in Verilog for asynchronous reset usually checks for positive edge of areset (posedge areset).
    // Let's implement standard async active-high reset.
    always @(posedge clk or posedge areset) begin
        if (areset) begin
            state <= S0;
        end else begin
            state <= next_state;
        end
    end

    // Combinational logic for next state and Moore output
    always @(*) begin
        case (state)
            S0: begin
                z = x; // 0 remains 0, first 1 remains 1
                if (x == 1'b1)
                    next_state = S1;
                else
                    next_state = S0;
            end

            S1: begin
                z = ~x; // invert all subsequent bits after the first 1
                next_state = S1;
            end

            default: begin
                z = 1'b0;
                next_state = S0;
            end
        endcase
    end

endmodule
```

